  },
  "vault_search": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "description": "Request body for `vault_search`.\n\n## Optional fields (backward-compatible)\n\n- `locus`: filter by physical path prefix (e.g. `\"council/\"` restricts to notes\n  whose `locus` starts with `council/`). Applied to both FTS and semantic paths.\n  The prefix is escaped against LIKE injection (metacharacters `%`, `_`, `\\`).\n- `vault_id`: cross-vault read — allows querying a vault other than `tenant_id`.\n  Writes remain unchanged (single-tenant). Validation: non-empty, max 128 chars.",
    "properties": {
      "include_corpus_count": {
        "default": false,
        "description": "If `true`, includes in the response the total count of notes matching\nthe **FTS5/BM25 lexical** query within the filtered scope, unbounded by K.\n\nAllows distinguishing \"topic absent from the corpus\" (`corpus_match_count == 0`)\nfrom \"notes present but ranked below K\" (`corpus_match_count > len(results)`).\n\nDoes NOT indicate semantic ANN hit count.\nOpt-in (default `false`): zero overhead when absent — no COUNT is executed.",
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "include_downgraded": {
        "default": false,
        "description": "If `true`, includes notes with `status = 'downgraded'`\nin the results with a penalized BM25 score (×0.1). Default `false`.",
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "include_scores": {
        "default": false,
        "description": "If `true`, enriches each result with a `scores` object detailing\nthe composite score breakdown.\n\nOpt-in (default `false`): only consumers that need it pay the payload overhead.\nExisting clients are unaffected — the `scores` field is omitted from the\nresponse when `false`.",
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "limit": {
        "description": "Maximum number of results (default 10, max 50).",
        "format": "uint32",
        "minimum": 0,
        "type": [
          "integer",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "locus": {
        "description": "locus prefix filter (optional).\n\nE.g. `\"council/\"` → restricts to notes whose `locus` starts with\n`council/`. LIKE metacharacters (`%`, `_`, `\\`) are automatically\nescaped — no SQL injection risk.\n\nAbsent or `null`: no locus filter (unchanged behavior).",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "query": {
        "description": "Full-text or semantic search query.",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "section": {
        "description": "Section filter (optional).",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "status": {
        "description": "Lifecycle status filter (optional).\n\nAccepted values: the 6 kebab-case `NoteStatus` variants (`draft`, `staging`,\n`pending-review`, `live`, `deprecated`, `garbage`) plus the legacy SQL value\n`downgraded` (tolerated for backward-compatible filtering). Any other value\n→ `400 Bad Request`. Applied at the SQL level (FTS + semantic), consistent\nwith the `section` filter.\n\nAbsent or `null`: no status filter (unchanged behavior).",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "tenant_id": {
        "default": "main",
        "description": "Tenant identifier (default `\"main\"`).",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "vault_id": {
        "description": "vault to query in read mode (optional).\n\nLifts the single-tenant constraint **for reads only** — allows querying\na vault other than `tenant_id`. Writes remain unchanged.\nValidation: non-empty, max 128 chars.\n\nAbsent or `null`: uses `tenant_id` (unchanged behavior).",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "query"
    ],
    "title": "VaultSearchRequest",
    "type": "object"
  },
  "vault_status": {
    "properties": {},
    "type": "object"
  },
  "vault_tags": {
    "properties": {},
    "type": "object"
  },
  "vault_timeline": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "description": "Request body for `vault_timeline` — paginated temporal read.\n\nAll fields are optional except defaults. Server sort order: `anchor_ms DESC,\nnote_id DESC`.\n\n## Validity windowing\n\nThe `(as_of_ms, include_expired)` pair controls temporal filtering:\n\n| `as_of_ms` | `include_expired` | Behavior |\n|---|---|---|\n| absent | `false` (default) | No filter — **baseline behavior** |\n| absent | `true` | No filter (`include_expired` has no effect without reference T) |\n| present | `false` (default) | Strict filter: notes valid at T |\n| present | `true` | Historical filter: notes created before T, including expired |",
    "properties": {
      "as_of_ms": {
        "description": "As-of reference instant for validity filtering (epoch ms UTC).\n\nActivates temporal filtering. Combined with `include_expired`:\n\n- `as_of_ms=t, include_expired=false` (default): **strict filter** — notes valid at T\n  (`anchor_ms ≤ t AND (valid_until IS NULL OR t < valid_until)`).\n- `as_of_ms=t, include_expired=true`: **historical filter** — notes created before T,\n  including expired ones (`anchor_ms ≤ t` only). Useful for reconstructing past state.\n- absent: no validity filter (unchanged baseline behavior).",
        "format": "int64",
        "type": [
          "integer",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "cursor": {
        "description": "Opaque pagination cursor (obtained from `next_cursor`).",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "doc_kind": {
        "description": "`doc_kind` filter (`\"Static\"` / `\"Event\"`). Absent = all.",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": [
          "array",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "from_ms": {
        "description": "Lower bound on `anchor_ms`, inclusive (epoch ms).",
        "format": "int64",
        "type": [
          "integer",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "include_expired": {
        "default": false,
        "description": "Enables inclusion of expired notes **when `as_of_ms` is present**.\n\nDefault `false`. No effect if `as_of_ms` is absent.\n\n`true` → historical filter: `anchor_ms ≤ t` only (notes expired at T\nare included — useful for reconstructing a past state).",
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "limit": {
        "description": "Maximum number of rows (default 50, clamped to max 200 server-side).",
        "format": "uint32",
        "minimum": 0,
        "type": [
          "integer",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "tenant_id": {
        "default": "main",
        "description": "Tenant (default `\"main\"`).",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "to_ms": {
        "description": "Upper bound on `anchor_ms`, inclusive (epoch ms).",
        "format": "int64",
        "type": [
          "integer",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "vault_id": {
        "description": "vault to query in read mode (default = `tenant_id`). Max 128 chars.",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      }
    },
    "title": "VaultTimelineRequest",
    "type": "object"
  },
  "vault_trace": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "description": "Request body for `vault_trace` — legacy vault v1.6.2 `VaultTraceArgs` parity.",
    "properties": {
      "limit": {
        "description": "Result limit (default 20, max 100).",
        "format": "uint32",
        "minimum": 0,
        "type": [
          "integer",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "query": {
        "description": "Trace query (tags, sections, pattern).",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "tenant_id": {
        "default": "main",
        "description": "Tenant identifier (default `\"main\"`).",
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "query"
    ],
    "title": "VaultTraceRequest",
    "type": "object"
  },
  "vault_write": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "description": "Request body for `vault_write` — creates a note via the async queue.\n\nSerialized via `bincode::serde::encode_to_vec` for the queue payload.",
    "properties": {
      "author": {
        "default": null,
        "description": "Author (optional).",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "body": {
        "description": "Markdown body of the note.",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "expected_sha256": {
        "default": null,
        "description": "Expected SHA-256 hash for optimistic locking (optional, hexadecimal).\n\nWhen present, the worker checks that the current hash of the note matches\nbefore writing. On mismatch: terminal job `Conflict` (note not overwritten).\n`None` = unconditional write (backward-compatible).\n\nFormat: 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters (SHA-256 = 32 bytes).\nExample: `\"a3f1c2d4...\"`",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "note_id": {
        "default": null,
        "description": "Pre-allocated ULID — honored by the legacy `SqliteQueue` dispatcher if present\nand parseable as a valid ULID.\n\n`None` = backward-compatible behavior: the dispatcher generates a fresh ULID.\n\n## Bincode field-order invariant\n\nThis field is at **position 8** (last) — AFTER `tenant_id` (pos 6) and\n`expected_sha256` (pos 7). Bincode v2 (`config::standard()`) is positional:\ndeclaration order determines serialization order.\nNever move this field without updating all encoders.",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "section_hint": {
        "default": null,
        "description": "Suggested section (optional — the curator may override).",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "tags": {
        "default": [],
        "description": "Initial tags (optional — the curator may add more).",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": "array"
      },
      "tenant_id": {
        "default": "main",
        "description": "Target tenant (default `\"main\"`).",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "title": {
        "description": "Title of the note.",
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "title",
      "body"
    ],
    "title": "VaultWriteRequest",
    "type": "object"
  }
}
